# =============================================================================
# loans-service SECRET TEMPLATE — copy to deploy/cells/loans.<iso>.local.env
# =============================================================================
#
# The keys the Secret `loans-service-secrets` may carry. It is the loans pod's
# ONLY envFrom source (deploy/k8s/loans/loans-service.yaml): loans never takes
# cell-zw / cell-zw-secrets whole — only the few keys its Deployment names —
# because Spring binds env vars onto properties by name and the cell's
# JWT_SECRET, BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD and SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE would land on
# loans' own. For the same reason, NONE of
# these keys ever goes into cell.<iso>.env or cell.<iso>.local.env: every fleet
# pod receives those, and the INNBUCKS_* credentials below book loans that
# InnBucks pays out.
#
# This file is committed and holds NO values. The real one is created on the
# host only (deploy/cells/*.local.env is gitignored), chmod 600:
#   cp deploy/cells/loans.example.env deploy/cells/loans.zw.local.env
# and loaded as in deploy/k8s/README.md ("loans-service"):
#   kubectl -n ticketing create secret generic loans-service-secrets \
#     --from-env-file=deploy/cells/loans.zw.local.env --dry-run=client -o yaml | kubectl apply -f -
#
# Format: KEY=value, one per line, no quotes and no trailing comment
# (--from-env-file keeps everything after the `=`). Lines starting with # are
# skipped. A key written as `KEY=` with nothing after it is NOT the same as
# leaving it out: it is set, to an empty string, and replaces the packaged
# default. So every optional key below is commented out; uncomment only the
# ones this host sets.
#
# ONLY the keys listed below belong in this file — never a SPRING_*, SERVER_*,
# DB_* or JAVA_* key. The port, the database, the profile, the country, the
# edge prefix and the WhatsApp gateway URL are explicit `env:` entries in the
# Deployment, but an explicit entry wins over this Secret for the SAME key only:
# Spring reaches one property through several names, so SPRING_DATASOURCE_URL
# here would repoint loans at another database (as the cell postgres
# superuser), and a profile line such as SPRING_PROFILES_GROUP_API=scheduled-tasks
# would switch on the jobs that pay out and lodge deductions.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# loans' OWN token-signing key (HS256, at least 32 bytes). Generate it with
# `openssl rand -base64 48`. NEVER the fleet's JWT_SECRET: a holder of a shared
# key can mint tokens for both systems. Loans refuses to boot without one.
JWT_SECRET=

# Password of the loans SUPER_ADMIN `admin`, created on the first boot against
# an empty loans_service database (loans' own, never the fleet's). Read only
# while no `admin` user exists; clear it after the first boot, as the fleet
# does with its own.
BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional — left out, the feature is off (or keeps its packaged default)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# InnBucks: loan booking and the payout deposit. The API's manual disbursement
# calls InnBucks too, so these are live even with the scheduled jobs off.
# INNBUCKS_API_KEY=
# INNBUCKS_USERNAME=
# INNBUCKS_PASSWORD=
# Packaged default: https://staging.innbucks.co.zw. Set only to change it.
# INNBUCKS_BASE_URL=
# The InnBucks loan product bookings are made against. Packaged default: NANOUS.
# INNBUCKS_LOAN_PRODUCT=

# Ndasenda payroll deductions. Used by the lodgement/commit/response jobs,
# which stay off in the cell until their own go-live step.
# NDASENDA_USERNAME=
# NDASENDA_PASSWORD=
# NDASENDA_SECURITY_CODE=
# NDASENDA_DEDUCTION_CODE=

# InnBucks notification API (email). The platform API the fleet sends through;
# the cell holds its values as BANK_API_URL / _KEY / _USERNAME / _PASSWORD.
# INNBUCKS_NOTIFY_URL=
# INNBUCKS_NOTIFY_API_KEY=
# INNBUCKS_NOTIFY_USERNAME=
# INNBUCKS_NOTIFY_PASSWORD=

# WhatsApp gateway key (the URL comes from the cell, see the Deployment).
# WHATSAPP_API_KEY=

# Deliberately absent: INNBUCKS_GATEWAY_URL. Loans' SMS client posts to the
# InnBucks core gateway adapter, and the only value the cell knows for it is a
# retired host. Left out, each loans SMS fails and is logged (never failing the
# request it belongs to) instead of carrying loans' API key to that host.
# So NO password loans sends by SMS reaches anyone in the cell: the one a new
# user is created with, and the one forgot-password would set (the gateway
# edge-denies that endpoint for this reason). A super-admin hands a user a
# password through loans' authenticated password reset over EMAIL or WHATSAPP,
# which need the INNBUCKS_NOTIFY_* or WHATSAPP_API_KEY keys above.
#
# Every other loans setting (JWT_EXPIRATION_MS, ACCOUNT_LOCKOUT_*, DOCUMENT_*,
# HTTP_CLIENT_*_MS, ...) keeps its packaged default; add it here only to change
# it.
